# GENERATED FILES THAT ARE HASHED BY CONTENT MUST NOT HAVE THEIR LINE ENDINGS
# REWRITTEN, and this file exists because that cost an operator a run.
#
# 2026-08-31: `toolkit/clientscan/movehook/sites.h` is written by gensites.py with
# LF endings, and build.ps1 stamps the sha256 of its BYTES into the DLL so that
# attach.py can refuse to inject a DLL built against a different site table. That
# refusal is correct and load-bearing -- arming a breakpoint from a stale table
# puts an 0xCC somewhere that is no longer the instruction the row names.
#
# But git's autocrlf checked the file out as CRLF, so a fresh checkout of an
# UNCHANGED file hashed differently from the one the DLL was built against. The
# operator got "movehook.dll was built against a DIFFERENT sites.h" on a tree
# where nothing had been edited, mid-run, and the recovery command printed with it
# used `&&` and could not run in PowerShell either.
#
# Pinning the generated header to LF makes the hash a fact about the site table
# rather than about which tree checked it out. Anything else generated-and-hashed
# belongs here too.
toolkit/clientscan/movehook/sites.h text eol=lf
